WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.760
The Matrix is one of the most influential
action movies of all time, but by mixing stylish

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.620
gun-fu fight scenes with cyberpunk themes,
it built to a trilogy that may have left a

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.700
few moviegoers a little confused.

00:00:13.049 --> 00:00:16.820
Now that we've got some distance from the
climactic installment, let's take a look back

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.240
at the movies' meaning and break down the
conclusion.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.080
Here's the ending of the Matrix trilogy explained.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:27.400
One major theme that came to the fore as the
series reached its conclusion had to do with

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.070
the similarities between humans and machines.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:34.531
In the original, they couldn't seem more different,
but by Revolutions, programs in the Matrix

00:00:34.531 --> 00:00:39.470
are portrayed as being almost more human than
our heroes, loving and happy individuals,

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.560
as worthy of existence as any person.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:46.080
Further, characters from the first film who
were firmly human or machine are portrayed

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.340
in the sequels as having a little bit of both.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.000
The similarities go in both directions.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.380
Agent Smith, a program, copied his consciousness
onto a human form, entering the real world

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.870
through the vessel of a resistance fighter
named Bane.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:03.660
Neo, a human, reached the Source to discover
that being the One was his destiny because

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.060
it was programmed into him.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:10.300
The humanizing of the Machines and the complimentary
mechanization of Neo made for a storytelling

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.780
turn that audiences weren't really ready for.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.500
People who saw The Matrix couldn't be faulted
for expecting an ending that saw Neo winning

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.720
by doing his Superman thing and eradicating
humanity’s robot overlords.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:26.820
Instead, Neo triumphed by becoming a bridge
between man and machine, sacrificing his own

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.880
life for the sake of securing the future.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:32.520
"What do you want?"

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:35.060
"Peace."

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:39.680
He also made Hugo Weaving’s head explode,
but that wasn’t quite as important.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.740
One widespread but inaccurate theory about
the sequels is that the “real world” is

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.330
actually a second Matrix.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.039
While the reasons why this isn't true are
explained in the movies, they're also relatively

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.300
easy to misunderstand.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:57.060
The real world isn't another level of the
Matrix, but it is involved in another system

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:57.740
of control.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:02.600
As the Architect explains at the ending of
The Matrix Reloaded, each version of the Matrix

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:06.189
is propped up in the real world by a controlled
rebellion.

00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:10.710
With each new iteration of the Matrix, a select
portion of the population is freed, allowed

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:12.000
to live in Zion.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.000
There, they help to liberate people still
inside the Matrix, searching for the One.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:20.460
Finding the One, the human rebels rally behind
them, supporting them until they reach the

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:20.960
Source.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.420
There, the One discovers that they are not
meant to destroy the Matrix, but rather restart

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:25.920
it.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.660
At this point in the cycle, the Machines attack
Zion and destroy it, killing the rebellion.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:35.220
The One, having reached the Source, is made
to choose between either reloading the Matrix

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:40.450
and selecting a handful of survivors to build
a new Zion, or walking away, supposedly causing

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:44.660
a system crash, leaving the humans inside
and outside of the Matrix all dead.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:50.360
Up until Neo, every One made the choice to
restart, perpetuating the system of control.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:54.600
Because Neo loves Trinity, he chooses to sacrifice
everything to be with her.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.580
This is the choice that makes him special.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:01.680
Proponents of the second Matrix theory support
it by pointing to the powers Neo is able to

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:06.710
manifest in the sequels' real world, being
able to see without eyes and exert control

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:08.160
over approaching Sentinels.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:12.080
For a lot of viewers, this breaking of the
rules almost felt like a betrayal, with the

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.250
audience having been made to believe that
Neo could only manifest his "superpowers"

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.060
in the Matrix.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.960
But Neo isn't able to destroy Sentinels because
he's the One, it's because he reached the

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:22.640
Source.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:27.720
Prior to the arrival of the Sentinels at the
ending of The Matrix Reloaded, Neo explained

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.180
that he could "feel them" before he remotely
destroyed them with his mind.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.420
By that point, Neo has literally established
a connection with everything else connected

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:38.040
to the Source, like the Machines themselves.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.860
He has, essentially, joined their wireless
network.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:45.780
It's why he's able to navigate the Machine
City, or see Smith inside of Bane during their

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:50.120
fight, Smith is of the machines, connected
to the Source just as Neo is.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.900
Thanks to that handy conduit, he doesn't need
eyes to kick Smith's butt.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.290
In the original Matrix, Agent Smith's character
was his job description, an agent for the

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.580
Matrix who aims to police the populace by
stomping down any signs of rebellion.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.420
"A virus.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.900
Human beings are a disease.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.420
A cancer of this planet."

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:17.820
After his encounter with Neo, however, Smith
begins to rebel himself and becomes much scarier

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:21.300
and more powerful as a rogue program than
he ever was as an Agent.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:26.080
In the second and third movies of the trilogy,
Neo and Smith become mirror images of each

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:30.199
other, with Neo gaining a connection to the
Matrix through the Source, and Smith gaining

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.300
a connection to the real world through his
override of Bane's brain.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:38.990
If Smith is the Matrix's virus, then Neo is
his natural anti-virus, a connection which

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:41.960
the Oracle makes clear during her final talk
with Neo.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:46.740
When Neo blew Smith apart at the ending of
The Matrix, he made a massive imprint on the

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:47.240
program.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:52.200
As a part of the Matrix's attempt to, as the
Oracle explained it, "balance the equation,"

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:56.380
Smith gained new attributes, overriding everything
in an effort to combat Neo.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.620
The fact that his spread is destructive to
the Matrix doesn't matter to Smith anymore.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:05.840
He's a rogue program now, cut loose from Machine
control, with his only purpose being to propagate

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:06.340
himself.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:08.480
He doesn't know why, and doesn't choose to
do it.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.940
It is, quite simply, his purpose.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:16.180
When Neo arrives at the Machine City, he's
met by what is, essentially, the collective

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:17.440
voice of the Machines.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:22.340
Well, first he watches Trinity die for about
35 minutes, you remember that fun scene.

00:05:22.349 --> 00:05:27.080
Anyway, in the Machine City the interconnected
hive mind adopts a human face to speak to

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:30.180
the first human ever to set foot inside the
city's walls.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:35.460
Neo approaches the Machines with a deal: He
knows that Smith is ravaging the Matrix, corrupting

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:38.040
everything, taking control of the entire system.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:43.260
The rogue program is a mutual enemy of both
species, and Neo offers to handle the problem

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:45.540
in exchange for one thing: peace.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:50.520
By this point in the story, the Machines'
usual plan for the Matrix is in utter disarray.

00:05:50.539 --> 00:05:54.919
Neo, having made his choice not to reload
the system upon arriving at the Source, is

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.760
now in totally new territory.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:01.740
He's already broken the loop, but still needs
to accomplish two goals: saving humanity from

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.520
the machines and saving the machines from
Smith.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:08.020
If he fails, everyone dies, there will be
only Smith.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:13.300
When Neo enters the Matrix for his gigantic
Super Saiyan battle, he doesn't do it with

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.940
the goal of beating Smith to death.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:15.780
How could he?

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:17.780
Smith is everywhere and everyone.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:23.340
Neo and the prime Smith battle as Smith's
limitless ranks look on, but Neo doesn't best

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:24.360
the program in the fight.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.040
He doesn't even come close.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:29.559
Before finishing him off, though, Smith has
one final question for Neo.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:30.140
"Why?

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.420
Why do you persist?"

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.140
"Because I choose to."

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:41.400
Smith, for all his power, cannot comprehend
the concept of choice.

00:06:41.409 --> 00:06:46.590
He is a creature of purpose, copying himself
mindlessly as a force of corruption, a symptom

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.639
of the Matrix desperately trying to balance
itself out.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:52.840
It’s Smith, not humanity, that has become
the virus.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:57.520
It's the choice to fight, rather than the
fight itself, that makes Neo win the battle.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:01.849
Neo doesn't succeed by coming out on top,
he wins by taking the battle with Smith to

00:07:01.849 --> 00:07:06.469
the very end and choosing to sacrifice himself
by letting Smith copy over him.

00:07:06.469 --> 00:07:08.740
The anti-virus cancels out the virus.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:12.999
If Smith had a choice, he wouldn't have done
it, but Smith doesn't have a choice.

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:18.680
He only has purpose, and he successfully fulfills
it, which is why, as he dies, all he can say

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:20.340
is that the outcome is not fair.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:25.860
The Matrix series ends not on a celebration
in the real world, but on a moment of reflection

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:29.100
among programs inside the seventh version
of the Matrix.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:34.120
With Smith destroyed, the revived Oracle sits
and waits for the sun rise as the Architect

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:34.620
approaches.

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:39.820
This is what it's always been about, this
battle between two programs, a yin and a yang.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:44.150
The cold philosophy of the Architect and the
faith of the Oracle have been driving the

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:48.509
conflict since its beginning, and now they
meet in a condition of cease fire.

00:07:48.509 --> 00:07:52.919
The series doesn't really explain all the
details of it, but Neo's defeat of Smith is

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:55.620
ultimately all the result of the Oracle's
intervention.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:00.860
In the first movie, the Oracle basically serves
as matchmaker between Neo and Trinity, telling

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:02.980
them it's their destiny to fall in love.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:04.240
Is it really, though?

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:09.500
Well, no, if the sequels make one thing clear,
it's that nobody is really destined to do

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:10.060
anything.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:11.360
It's all about choice.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:16.360
The Oracle's encouragement of Neo and Trinity's
romance provides the rogue element that lets

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:19.720
Neo break out of the cycle of control when
he reaches the Source.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:24.400
Instead of reloading the Matrix, he leaves
to be with Trinity, forget the consequences.

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:28.319
It was Neo's choice, sure, but it was also
part of the Oracle's plan.

00:08:28.319 --> 00:08:34.110
"What’s really going to bake your noodle
later on is, would you still have broken it

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.160
if I hadn’t said anything?"

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:36.880
Did she know it would work?

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:39.120
No, but she believed, and she was right.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.960
The element of love was the one thing the
Machines couldn't prepare for.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:48.140
One of the most curious and under-explained
characters in the Matrix sequels is the young

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:52.540
girl, who is treated with much importance
without the why of it all really being explained.

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:58.000
The daughter of two programs Neo meets inside
the Trainman's purgatory, Sati is a program

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:01.639
without purpose, born as the result of love
between two individuals.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:07.320
In the machine world, such an entity is a
novelty, and also useless, subject to deletion,

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:10.200
which is why Sati's parents are trying to
shepherd her to shelter.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:14.740
Thematically, Sati is the representation of
love, a new concept to the Machines.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:19.060
Love, at the end of the series, is ultimately
what secures the humans' victory.

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:23.920
Neo's love for Trinity is what drives him
to make the choice to reject reloading the

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:26.120
Matrix, and instead fight for a better peace.

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:30.670
The Machines' inability to comprehend love
left them with that blind spot, allowing Neo

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:34.420
to go against every logical choice to make
his own choices instead.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:37.820
Sati can be seen as the Machines' way of trying
to make sense of love.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:41.960
At the end of the movie, she is essentially
what the Machines have decided to let control

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:46.270
the Matrix, with the Architect and Oracle's
conflict being set aside for the system's

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.100
seventh version.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:52.100
This, at least, is pretty much confirmed by
the beautiful sunrise Sati said she made for

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:56.560
Neo, and is supported by the new, compassionate
approach to the Matrix's human population

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:57.300
in the new version.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:58.960
"Did you do that?"

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:01.320
"For Neo."

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:05.760
The ending of The Matrix trilogy doesn't see
the Matrix destroyed.

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:10.580
In fact, it is renewed, rebooted for a seventh
version, this time with new rules.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:15.240
As audiences learned via the lengthy conversation
with the Architect in The Matrix Reloaded,

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:19.720
previous iterations of the Matrix all built
on the flaws of the previous one, fine-tuning

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:24.460
the system by which the Machines controlled
humanity both inside and outside of the Matrix.

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:27.980
"Ere go, concordantly, vis a vis…

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:29.880
You know what?

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:32.740
I have no idea what the hell I'm saying.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:35.020
I just thought it would make me sound cool."

00:10:35.029 --> 00:10:39.470
With a peace secured and a new compassionate
approach at hand, any human who desires to

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:41.620
depart the Matrix will be allowed to leave.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:46.480
Certainly, some will stay, the Matrix is the
ultimate virtual reality game, after all,

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:49.860
but the conditions of enslavement are no more,
at least for now.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:53.680
The end of the movie implies that more cycles
may be set to come.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:57.899
As the Oracle explained, the peace between
the warring humans and Machines will only

00:10:57.899 --> 00:10:59.680
last "as long as it can."

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:03.040
The peace is not guaranteed, the Architect
makes that clear.

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:07.840
Sati's mere existence is proof that the Machines
are now working to understand this little

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:11.420
thing called love, letting her steer the ship
while they observe and learn.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:16.660
Maybe, at some point, forces within the Matrix
will figure out how to use love against humanity

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:17.940
and enslave them again.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:21.160
Until then, it's a beautiful morning in the
Matrix and beyond.

